{"findings":[{"rule_id":"MF-005","evidence":[{"kind":"title_block","ref":"heat_treatment","page":1,"quote":"TO BE TEMPERED UPTO 24-32 HRC."}],"comment":"The heat treatment specifies tempering to 24-32 HRC but does not state at which manufacturing stage it applies (e.g., after rough machining, before final grinding). Without a defined stage the shop cannot sequence operations correctly, risking distortion of finished features or inability to machine hardened stock. The designer should add the process stage to the heat treatment callout in the title block or note N1."
  , "recommended_correction": "Update the heat_treatment field or note N1 to specify when tempering occurs relative to machining and surface treatment."},{"rule_id":"WPS-004","evidence":[{"kind":"dimension","ref":"D24","page":1,"quote":"⌀8   H7 THRU`"},{"kind":"title_block","ref":"surface_treatment","page":1,"quote":"I.Z.B.P. (TRIVALENT)"}],"comment":"The ⌀8 H7 through holes (D24) are a tight fit, yet the part carries an I.Z.B.P. plating callout with no allowance for coating thickness on those holes. Plating buildup will shrink the bore below the H7 limit and prevent assembly of the mating pin. The designer should either mask the H7 holes during plating, ream them after plating, or adjust the pre-plate tolerance to account for the expected coating thickness."
  , "recommended_correction": "Add a masking note for the H7 holes, specify post-plate reaming, or open the pre-plate hole tolerance by the plating thickness per WPS-004."}]}
